SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 62, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "62", "printedPageNumber": 62, "pdfPageNumber": 445, "sequenceIndex": 52, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [{"id": "b0620100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "parentId": null, "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith II", "sourceIdentifier": "II", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "f0620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Virtues of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 62"}, {"id": "f0620100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "at his place does absolve himself of the obligation. But in the opinion of some of the companions and their successors, salaat with jamaat (after hearing the Azaan) is fardh and its discard is haraam. According to many other theologians, such a person is not even absolved of the obligation in respect of salaat of that hour. Anyhow, he is surely committing the sin of discarding jamaat. In another hadith narrated by Hadhrat Ibn Abbas, it is stated that such a person is guilty of disobedience of Allah and His Apostle (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam). Hadhrat Ibn Abbas (Radhiyallaho anho) also says, \"No good is done by, nor any good is done to, the person who does not join jamaat after hearing the Azaan.\" Hadhrat Abu Hurairah (Radhiyallaho anho) says, \"It is more appropriate to pour molten-lead into the ears of a person who does not go to join jamaat.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 62"}, {"id": "f0620200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0620100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith II", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": false, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 62"}, {"id": "f0620300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0620100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "قال العلماء كل من سمع النداء فلم يجب فلا صلاة له وقال ﷺ بحسب المؤمن من الشقاء والخيبة أن يسمع المؤذن يثوب بالصلاة فلا يجيبه رواه الطبراني عن معاذ بن أنس كذا في الكنز", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 62"}, {"id": "f0620400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0620100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "translation", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Mu''aaz bin Anas (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"A person who does not go for salaat after hearing the Azaan is committing a great wrong and is doing an act of kufr and nifaaq.\"\n\nAccording to this hadith, not to join jamaat after hearing the Azaan is not becoming of a Muslim and is the practice of a kaafir or a munaafiq. What a strong reproof!\n\nIn another hadith, it is said, \"Not to join jamaat after hearing the Azaan is sufficient to render a person most unfortunate and most wretched.\"\n\nHadhrat Sulaimaan bin Abi Hathmah (Radhiyallaho anho) is one of the eminent people of the early days of Islam. He was born during the lifetime of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam), but was too young then to have had the honour of listening to any hadith from him. During the Caliphate of Hadhrat Umar (Radhiyallaho anho) he was made in charge of the market. One day Hadhrat Umar (Radhiyallaho anho) found him missing in Fajr salaat. Hadhrat Umar (Radhiyallaho anho) went to his house and inquired from his mother why Sulaimaan was not present in Fajr. She replied, \"He kept saying nafl salaat throughout the", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 62"}]}'::jsonb);